#, rust-format
#~ msgid "Same supervisor: see {}"
#~ msgstr "同一个总管：见 {}"

#~ msgid "Kept you waiting today"
#~ msgstr "今天让你等过的"

#, rust-format
#~ msgid "{} min"
#~ msgstr "{} 分"

#~ msgid "now"
#~ msgstr "现在"

#~ msgid "Role Editor (beta)..."
#~ msgstr "角色编辑器（beta）…"

# Chosen by error_kind, never by reading the core's message. The core's own text follows this line, because ours says that something is wrong and only the core's says which line.
#~ msgid ""
#~ "The roles file could not be read, so the previous one is still in use"
#~ msgstr "角色文件读不出来，现在用的还是上一份"

# Beside an MCP row whose slot process is broken. It must not read as «switched off by hand»: the user did not do it, and the place to go is the server, not the persona.
#~ msgid "This server didn't start. Your role isn't what's withholding it."
#~ msgstr "这个服务器没有起来。不是你的角色没给你它。"

# The `transparent` slot state. Only two of the four states speak: granted and withheld are what the checkbox already shows, and a sentence on every row would drown the one that matters.
#~ msgid "Polter isn't managing this server, so the agent sees all of it"
#~ msgstr "Polter 没有接管这个服务器，所以 agent 看得到它的全部"

#~ msgid "Added by hand"
#~ msgstr "手动加上的"

# The other direction from «Added by hand». Both are departures from the persona, but the user undoes them with opposite actions, so they are two phrases and not one.
#~ msgid "Switched off by hand"
#~ msgstr "手动关掉的"

# Our gap, not the agent's. The reader should go and check the path, not go and install something.
#~ msgid "Nobody has checked where this agent keeps these yet"
#~ msgstr "还没有人核实过这家 agent 把它们放在哪"

# Shared deliberately by two states -- the path is known and empty, and the path was read and held nothing. To the user those are one fact.
#~ msgid "Looked there, and nothing is installed"
#~ msgstr "去那儿看过了，那里什么都没装"

# It is there and could not be parsed. The core's own detail is shown beside this.
#~ msgid "Couldn't read what's installed here"
#~ msgstr "这儿装了什么，读不出来"

#~ msgid "Reset to the Role"
#~ msgstr "恢复成这个角色的样子"

#~ msgid "What This Terminal Hands Out"
#~ msgstr "这个终端交出去的东西"

# The third of three «nothing has reported» sentences. The other two are about which roles exist and what is installed on this machine; they are three different facts and must not share one phrase.
#~ msgid "Nothing has reported what this terminal hands out yet"
#~ msgstr "还没有人报上来这个终端交出去了什么"

# Asked, and the answer was nothing -- as opposed to nobody having reported.
#~ msgid "This terminal hands out nothing yet"
#~ msgstr "这个终端还没有交出去任何东西"

#~ msgid "Opening Prompt"
#~ msgstr "开场提示词"

#~ msgid "Only Applied on Restart"
#~ msgstr "只有重启才兑现"

#~ msgid "Installed on This Machine"
#~ msgstr "这台机器上已经装了的"

# Must be on the page and not only in a code comment: a read-only list with no explanation sends the reader looking for switches that are deliberately absent.
#~ msgid ""
#~ "Shown so you can see what a role doesn't cover. Polter doesn't change any "
#~ "of this."
#~ msgstr "列在这里，是为了让你看见角色没有覆盖到哪里。Polter 不会动这些。"

# The third state again, for the read-only list. An empty list would be read as «nothing is installed on this machine».
#~ msgid "Nothing has reported what's installed here yet"
#~ msgstr "还没有人报上来这台机器装了什么"

# A number computed from an incomplete scan looks exactly like one computed from a complete scan, so the incompleteness has to be said out loud.
#~ msgid ""
